Likelihood
Suppose we have a random variable \(X\) whose distribution belongs to a known parametric family \(\{P_\theta:\theta\in\Theta\}\), with probability density or mass function \(f(x;\theta)\). The functional form of the distribution is known, but the parameter \(\theta\in\Theta\subseteq\mathbb R^p\) is unknown.
The most important approach using the observed data to obtain good estimates of the unknown parameter \(\theta\) is likelihood theory, which uses the probability model for the observed data to construct estimators and perform inference. The basic idea is to identify parameter values under which the observed data are relatively more plausible.






Definition (Likelihood Functions)



Suppose we observe data \(X_1,\ldots,X_n\) that are independent and identically distributed (i.i.d.) from a common density or probability mass function \(f(x;\theta)\). Under the i.i.d. assumption, the joint density of the sample is
\[
f(x_1,\ldots,x_n;\theta)
=
\prod_{i=1}^n f(x_i;\theta).
\]
Once the data \(x_1,\ldots,x_n\) are observed and treated as fixed, we can instead regard this expression as a function of the unknown parameter \(\theta\). This is called the likelihood function,
\[
L(\theta)
=
\prod_{i=1}^n f(x_i;\theta).
\]
Although the likelihood and joint density have the same mathematical expression, they are interpreted differently. A probability density describes how the data vary for a fixed parameter, whereas a likelihood describes how the relative support for different parameter values varies for fixed observed data.
In particular, the likelihood is not a probability distribution over \(\theta\) and need not integrate to one over the parameter space.


Because products can be difficult to work with, we usually take the logarithm to obtain the log-likelihood,
\[
\ell(\theta)
=
\log L(\theta)
=
\sum_{i=1}^n\log f(x_i;\theta).
\]
The logarithm is strictly increasing, so maximizing the likelihood is equivalent to maximizing the log-likelihood.


MLE
The maximum likelihood estimator (MLE) is defined as the parameter value that maximizes the likelihood of the observed data,
\[
\boxed{
\hat\theta
=
\arg\max_{\theta\in\Theta}L(\theta)
=
\arg\max_{\theta\in\Theta}\ell(\theta).
}
\]
The intuition is straightforward: among the parameter values allowed by our model, we select the one under which the observed data have the greatest likelihood.
Mathematically, this is an ordinary optimization problem. The functions being optimized now have special statistical names, but we can use the same tools from calculus and numerical optimization. For a scalar parameter \(\theta\), if the log-likelihood is differentiable and the maximum occurs in the interior of the parameter space, a necessary first-order condition is
\[
\frac{d\ell(\hat\theta)}{d\theta}=0.
\]
A negative second derivative at a stationary point,
\[
\frac{d^2\ell(\hat\theta)}{d\theta^2}&lt;0,
\]
establishes a strict local maximum. To establish a global maximum, we must also examine the overall shape of the likelihood and its behavior at the boundaries.

{
  // Maximum-likelihood exploration: self-contained Observable JS / Quarto.
  // No R packages, external JS libraries, or additional CSS are required.
  const C = {
    ink: "#35424d", muted: "#65727c", border: "#d9e0e5",
    grid: "#e9edf0", blue: "#287cb5", orange: "#ad651b",
    green: "#2a936d", purple: "#8955b7", surface: "#fbfcfe"
  };

  const state = {
    model: "bernoulli", n: 20, view: "relative",
    params: {
      bernoulli: {truth: 0.65, candidate: 0.35},
      normal: {truth: 0.6, candidate: -0.3}
    },
    u: [], z: []
  };

  function resample() {
    state.u = Array.from({length: 120}, () =&gt; Math.random());
    state.z = Array.from({length: 120}, () =&gt; {
      const u = Math.max(Math.random(), Number.MIN_VALUE);
      const v = Math.random();
      return Math.sqrt(-2 * Math.log(u)) * Math.cos(2 * Math.PI * v);
    });
  }
  resample();

  const root = html`&lt;section class="mle-lab"&gt;
    &lt;style&gt;
      .mle-lab { color:${C.ink}; background:${C.surface}; border:1px solid ${C.border};
        border-left:4px solid ${C.blue}; border-radius:9px; padding:16px;
        margin:1rem 0 1.4rem; font-family:var(--bs-body-font-family,system-ui,sans-serif); }
      .mle-lab * { box-sizing:border-box; }
      .mle-lab .mle-head {display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:baseline;
        gap:10px; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-bottom:13px;}
      .mle-lab .mle-title {font-weight:700; font-size:1.12rem;}
      .mle-lab .mle-sub {font-size:.85rem; color:${C.muted};}
      .mle-lab .mle-controls {display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.05fr 1fr 1fr 1fr;
        gap:12px; padding:13px; background:white; border:1px solid ${C.border}; border-radius:7px;}
      .mle-lab .mle-control {min-width:0; display:grid; gap:5px; align-content:start;}
      .mle-lab label {display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:baseline;
        flex-wrap:wrap; gap:4px; font-size:.86rem; font-weight:650;}
      .mle-lab label output {color:${C.blue}; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;}
      .mle-lab select {min-width:0; width:100%; background:white; color:${C.ink}; border:1px solid ${C.border};
        border-radius:5px; font:inherit; padding:6px 7px;}
      .mle-lab input[type=range] {width:100%; min-width:0; accent-color:${C.blue}; cursor:pointer;}
      .mle-lab input.mle-candidate {accent-color:${C.orange};}
      .mle-lab .mle-actions {display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center;
        gap:8px; flex-wrap:wrap; margin:11px 0 13px;}
      .mle-lab .mle-actions button {font:inherit; font-size:.87rem; cursor:pointer;
        border:1px solid #cdd6dc; background:white; color:${C.ink};
        border-radius:5px; padding:7px 11px;}
      .mle-lab .mle-actions button:hover {background:#eff6fb; border-color:${C.blue};}
      .mle-lab .mle-view {display:flex; align-items:center; gap:7px; font-size:.86rem;}
      .mle-lab .mle-view select {width:auto; max-width:205px;}
      .mle-lab .mle-panels {display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:12px;}
      .mle-lab .mle-panel {background:white; border:1px solid ${C.border};
        border-radius:7px; padding:11px; min-width:0;}
      .mle-lab .mle-panel-heading {font-size:.95rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:2px;}
      .mle-lab .mle-panel-desc {font-size:.81rem; color:${C.muted}; min-height:2.7em;}
      .mle-lab svg {width:100%; height:auto; display:block; overflow:visible;}
      .mle-lab .mle-likelihood-chart {cursor:crosshair;}
      .mle-lab .mle-key {display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:5px 13px;
        margin:5px 0 0; font-size:.79rem; color:${C.muted};}
      .mle-lab .mle-swatch {display:inline-block; width:13px; height:3px;
        margin-right:5px; vertical-align:middle; border-radius:1px;}
      .mle-lab .mle-summary {margin-top:13px; display:grid;
        grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:8px;}
      .mle-lab .mle-stat {background:white; border:1px solid ${C.border};
        border-radius:6px; padding:9px 10px; min-width:0;}
      .mle-lab .mle-stat-label {font-size:.76rem; color:${C.muted};}
      .mle-lab .mle-stat-value {font-weight:700; font-size:1.08rem;
        font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; overflow-wrap:anywhere;}
      .mle-lab .mle-formula {font-size:.89rem; line-height:1.7; margin-top:12px;
        background:white; border:1px solid ${C.border}; border-radius:6px; padding:10px 12px;}
      .mle-lab .mle-math {font-family:Georgia,Cambria,serif; font-size:1.04em;}
      .mle-lab .mle-foot {font-size:.83rem; color:${C.muted}; margin-top:9px; line-height:1.5;}
      @media (max-width:800px) {
        .mle-lab .mle-controls {grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;}
        .mle-lab .mle-panels {grid-template-columns:1fr;}
      }
      @media (max-width:460px) {
        .mle-lab {padding:11px;}
        .mle-lab .mle-summary {grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;}
      }
    &lt;/style&gt;

    &lt;div class="mle-head"&gt;
      &lt;span class="mle-title"&gt;Maximum likelihood estimation&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="mle-sub"&gt;Fix the sample; vary the proposed parameter&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;

    &lt;div class="mle-controls"&gt;
      &lt;div class="mle-control"&gt;
        &lt;label for="mle-model"&gt;Statistical model&lt;/label&gt;
        &lt;select class="mle-model" aria-label="Statistical model"&gt;
          &lt;option value="bernoulli"&gt;Bernoulli(p)&lt;/option&gt;
          &lt;option value="normal"&gt;Normal(μ, 1)&lt;/option&gt;
        &lt;/select&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;div class="mle-control"&gt;
        &lt;label&gt;Sample size &lt;output class="mle-n-text"&gt;&lt;/output&gt;&lt;/label&gt;
        &lt;input class="mle-n" type="range" min="5" max="100" step="1" value="20" aria-label="Sample size"&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;div class="mle-control"&gt;
        &lt;label&gt;Generating parameter &lt;output class="mle-truth-text"&gt;&lt;/output&gt;&lt;/label&gt;
        &lt;input class="mle-truth" type="range" aria-label="Generating parameter"&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;div class="mle-control"&gt;
        &lt;label&gt;Candidate parameter &lt;output class="mle-candidate-text"&gt;&lt;/output&gt;&lt;/label&gt;
        &lt;input class="mle-candidate" type="range" aria-label="Candidate parameter"&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;

    &lt;div class="mle-actions"&gt;
      &lt;div&gt;
        &lt;button class="mle-resample" type="button"&gt;New random sample&lt;/button&gt;
        &lt;button class="mle-setmle" type="button"&gt;Move candidate to MLE&lt;/button&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;div class="mle-view"&gt;
        &lt;label for="mle-scale"&gt;Show&lt;/label&gt;
        &lt;select class="mle-scale" aria-label="Likelihood scale"&gt;
          &lt;option value="relative"&gt;Relative likelihood&lt;/option&gt;
          &lt;option value="log"&gt;Log-likelihood difference&lt;/option&gt;
        &lt;/select&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;

    &lt;div class="mle-panels"&gt;
      &lt;div class="mle-panel"&gt;
        &lt;div class="mle-panel-heading"&gt;1. Observed sample&lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div class="mle-panel-desc mle-data-desc"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;svg class="mle-data-chart" viewBox="0 0 540 290" role="img" aria-label="Observed sample with fitted parameter"&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;div class="mle-panel"&gt;
        &lt;div class="mle-panel-heading"&gt;2. Likelihood as a function of the parameter&lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div class="mle-panel-desc"&gt;Click the plot to change the candidate parameter.&lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;svg class="mle-likelihood-chart" viewBox="0 0 540 290" role="img" aria-label="Likelihood curve and maximum likelihood estimate"&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;

    &lt;div class="mle-key"&gt;
      &lt;span&gt;&lt;i class="mle-swatch" style="background:${C.blue}"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;Likelihood curve / sample&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span&gt;&lt;i class="mle-swatch" style="background:${C.orange}"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;Candidate parameter&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span&gt;&lt;i class="mle-swatch" style="background:${C.green}"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;MLE (best fitting)&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span&gt;&lt;i class="mle-swatch" style="background:${C.purple}"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;Generating parameter&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;

    &lt;div class="mle-summary"&gt;
      &lt;div class="mle-stat"&gt;&lt;div class="mle-stat-label"&gt;Sample&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="mle-stat-value mle-sample"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;div class="mle-stat"&gt;&lt;div class="mle-stat-label"&gt;MLE&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="mle-stat-value mle-estimate"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;div class="mle-stat"&gt;&lt;div class="mle-stat-label"&gt;Candidate&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="mle-stat-value mle-proposal"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;div class="mle-stat"&gt;&lt;div class="mle-stat-label"&gt;Relative likelihood&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="mle-stat-value mle-ratio"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;

    &lt;div class="mle-formula"&gt;
      &lt;div class="mle-model-formula"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;div class="mle-numeric-formula"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class="mle-foot"&gt;
      The &lt;strong&gt;data are held fixed&lt;/strong&gt; as you move the candidate parameter. The likelihood
      measures how well each parameter value explains those same observations; it is
      &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; a probability distribution for the parameter. The generating value is
      shown only because this is a simulation, and it generally differs from the sample MLE.
      Increasing &lt;em&gt;n&lt;/em&gt; often makes the likelihood more concentrated.
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/section&gt;`;

  const $ = selector =&gt; root.querySelector(selector);
  const fmt = (x, digits = 3) =&gt; Number.isFinite(x)
    ? x.toFixed(digits).replace(/0+$/, "").replace(/\.$/, "") : "−∞";
  const clamp = (x, lo, hi) =&gt; Math.max(lo, Math.min(hi, x));
  const cfg = () =&gt; state.model === "bernoulli"
    ? {symbol:"p", min:0, max:1, tmin:.05, tmax:.95, step:.01}
    : {symbol:"μ", min:-3, max:3, tmin:-2, tmax:2, step:.01};
  const param = () =&gt; state.params[state.model];
  const sample = () =&gt; state.model === "bernoulli"
    ? state.u.slice(0,state.n).map(u =&gt; Number(u &lt; param().truth))
    : state.z.slice(0,state.n).map(z =&gt; z + param().truth);
  const mean = xs =&gt; xs.reduce((a,b) =&gt; a + b, 0) / xs.length;

  function logLike(theta, xs) {
    const n = xs.length;
    if (state.model === "normal") {
      return -n * Math.log(2*Math.PI)/2 - xs.reduce((s,x) =&gt; s + (x-theta)**2,0)/2;
    }
    const successes = xs.reduce((a,b) =&gt; a+b, 0);
    if ((theta === 0 && successes &gt; 0) || (theta === 1 && successes &lt; n)) return -Infinity;
    return (successes === 0 ? 0 : successes * Math.log(theta)) +
      (successes === n ? 0 : (n-successes) * Math.log1p(-theta));
  }

  // Pixel helpers shared by both SVG charts.
  const W = 540, H = 290, pad = {left:49, right:15, top:24, bottom:45};
  const iw = W-pad.left-pad.right, ih = H-pad.top-pad.bottom;
  const Sx = (x, a, b) =&gt; pad.left + (x-a)/(b-a)*iw;
  const Sy = (y, a, b) =&gt; pad.top + (b-y)/(b-a)*ih;
  const svgText = (x,y,s,attrs="") =&gt;
    `&lt;text x="${x}" y="${y}" ${attrs}&gt;${s}&lt;/text&gt;`;
  const clip = (name) =&gt; `&lt;defs&gt;&lt;clipPath id="${name}"&gt;&lt;rect x="${pad.left}" y="${pad.top}" width="${iw}" height="${ih}"/&gt;&lt;/clipPath&gt;&lt;/defs&gt;`;
  function grid(xTicks, yTicks, xa, xb, ya, yb, xLabel, yLabel, yFormatter=fmt) {
    let s = `&lt;rect x="${pad.left}" y="${pad.top}" width="${iw}" height="${ih}" fill="#fff" stroke="${C.border}"/&gt;`;
    for (const t of xTicks) {
      const x=Sx(t,xa,xb);
      s += `&lt;line x1="${x}" x2="${x}" y1="${pad.top}" y2="${pad.top+ih}" stroke="${C.grid}"/&gt;`;
      s += svgText(x,H-23,fmt(t,2),`font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="${C.muted}"`);
    }
    for (const t of yTicks) {
      const y=Sy(t,ya,yb);
      s += `&lt;line x1="${pad.left}" x2="${pad.left+iw}" y1="${y}" y2="${y}" stroke="${C.grid}"/&gt;`;
      s += svgText(pad.left-8,y+4,yFormatter(t),`font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="${C.muted}"`);
    }
    s += svgText(pad.left+iw,H-4,xLabel,`font-size="13" text-anchor="end" fill="${C.muted}"`);
    s += svgText(pad.left,14,yLabel,`font-size="13" fill="${C.muted}"`);
    return s;
  }
  function pathOf(fn, xa, xb, ya, yb, num=400) {
    let d="", pen=false;
    for (let i=0;i&lt;=num;i++) {
      const x=xa+(xb-xa)*i/num, y=fn(x);
      if (!Number.isFinite(y)) {pen=false; continue;}
      // Clip vertically via the chart clipPath. Coordinates remain finite.
      const py=Sy(clamp(y,ya-100,yb+100),ya,yb);
      d += `${pen?"L":"M"}${Sx(x,xa,xb).toFixed(2)},${py.toFixed(2)} `;
      pen=true;
    }
    return d;
  }

  function drawData(xs, thetaHat) {
    const theta=param().candidate, truth=param().truth;
    let s=clip("mle-data-clip")+`&lt;rect width="${W}" height="${H}" fill="white"/&gt;`;
    if (state.model==="bernoulli") {
      s += grid([1,Math.max(1,Math.round(state.n/4)),Math.max(1,Math.round(state.n/2)),
        Math.max(1,Math.round(3*state.n/4)),state.n].filter((t,i,a)=&gt;a.indexOf(t)===i),
        [0,.25,.5,.75,1],1,state.n,-.08,1.12,"Trial index","Outcome (0 or 1)",v=&gt;fmt(v,2));
      s += `&lt;g clip-path="url(#mle-data-clip)"&gt;`;
      for (const [y,color,dash] of [[truth,C.purple,"4 5"],[thetaHat,C.green,"7 4"],[theta,C.orange,""]]) {
        const py=Sy(y,-.08,1.12);
        s += `&lt;line x1="${pad.left}" y1="${py}" x2="${pad.left+iw}" y2="${py}" stroke="${color}" stroke-width="2" ${dash?`stroke-dasharray="${dash}"`:""} opacity=".85"/&gt;`;
      }
      xs.forEach((v,i)=&gt; {
        s += `&lt;circle cx="${Sx(i+1,1,state.n)}" cy="${Sy(v,-.08,1.12)}" r="${state.n&gt;65?3:4.3}" fill="${C.blue}" stroke="white" stroke-width=".75"/&gt;`;
      });
      s+=`&lt;/g&gt;`;
      $(".mle-data-desc").textContent =
        "Each blue dot is one 0/1 observation; horizontal lines show the proposed and fitted success probabilities.";
    } else {
      const xa=-5.3, xb=5.3, ya=0, yb=.56;
      const pdf=(x,mu)=&gt; Math.exp(-((x-mu)**2)/2)/Math.sqrt(2*Math.PI);
      s += grid([-4,-2,0,2,4],[0,.1,.2,.3,.4,.5],xa,xb,ya,yb,
        "Observed value x","Normal density",v=&gt;fmt(v,1));
      s += `&lt;g clip-path="url(#mle-data-clip)"&gt;`;
      for(const [mu,color,dash] of [[truth,C.purple,"5 5"],[thetaHat,C.green,"7 5"],[theta,C.orange,""]]){
        s += `&lt;path d="${pathOf(x=&gt;pdf(x,mu),xa,xb,ya,yb)}" fill="none" stroke="${color}" stroke-width="2.5" ${dash?`stroke-dasharray="${dash}"`:""}/&gt;`;
      }
      xs.forEach((x,i)=&gt;{
        const xx=Sx(x,xa,xb);
        const base=Sy(0,ya,yb);
        s += `&lt;line x1="${xx}" y1="${base}" x2="${xx}" y2="${base-11-(i%3)*3}" stroke="${C.blue}" stroke-width="1.3" opacity=".75"/&gt;`;
      });
      s += `&lt;/g&gt;`;
      $(".mle-data-desc").textContent =
        "Blue ticks are observations; curves are Normal densities with the candidate, fitted, and generating means.";
    }
    $(".mle-data-chart").innerHTML=s;
  }

  function drawLikelihood(xs, thetaHat) {
    const {min,max,symbol}=cfg(), theta=param().candidate, truth=param().truth;
